# What must never end up inside a generated, committed artifact.
#
# graphify has two modes and only one of them is safe here. `graphify . --code-only` indexes the
# AST and nothing else — that is how graphify-out/ has always been built, and it is what `batten
# doctor` tells you to run. Plain `graphify update .` also indexes docs, and GRAPH_REPORT.md's own
# "next steps" line recommends exactly that.
#
# That matters more than it looks. A machine-generated 2 MB JSON is unreviewable in a diff, which
# is the same reason .gitattributes marks it linguist-generated — so a generated file is the one
# place where something private can be committed and no human will ever see it. Two checks now
# look INSIDE it anyway (the tracked-token guard in ci.yml and internal/install), and both had to
# defeat two locks to get there: the `:!graphify-out` path exclusion, and `git grep -I`, which
# skips `-diff` files as binary.
#
# `docs/field-test/` was listed here — it held 328 verbatim references to a private project and
# was the exact payload this file existed to keep out of the graph. It was retired from the tree
# (decision 1.1, option A2), so the entry is gone rather than left as a rule about nothing.

# Personal working material. Same rule as .gitignore, restated here because a graph is built from
# the working tree, not from the index — an untracked file is still fair game for the extractor.
*.local.md
*.pdf
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
